<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darul Islam (Indonesia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Darul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was an Islamist rebel movement that fought to establish an Islamic State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Its leader Sekarmadji Maridjan Kartosuwiryo proclaimed the state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a> in 1949, and revolts in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, South Kalimantan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a>, where Daud Beureueh rose in 1953, joined it. The movement collapsed after Kartosuwiryo was captured and executed in 1962.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/darul-islam-indonesia.jpg" alt="Darul Islam (Indonesia)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Islamic State of Indonesia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Islamic_State_of_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The memory of independence and of long resistance to the Dutch remained central to Acehnese identity, feeding the <b>Darul Islam</b> revolt of the 1950s and the Free Aceh Movement, whose conflict with Indonesia ended in the Helsinki peace agreement of 2005, after which Aceh gained special autonomy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aceh-sultanate">Aceh Sultanate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1950s it suppressed regional rebellions, including the <b>Darul Islam</b> movement, which sought an Islamic state, and the PRRI and Permesta revolts in Sumatra and Sulawesi in 1958.</blockquote><a href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
